From 7c8b17b9829307e273e75263f89589f553dbbc92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:51:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] pluto_rx: port to the libiio 1.0 stream API

Scan with iio_scan, attributes through iio_attr, a channels mask and
iio_buffer_create_stream with the kernel buffer count as the number of
blocks. The registers 0x80000088 are still read and written with
iio_device_reg_read and iio_device_reg_write. The perf mode now sizes its
blocks in the same unit as the first stream. Tested on Pluto+ against a
tone from the Pluto: same samples as the 0.x build in 16 and 8 bit mode,
with 4, 64 blocks and the default.

Signed-off-by: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
---
